   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How many hours can a dog hold their pee?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The common guideline is about their age in months + 1 hour for puppies, and a chance at least once every 6 to 8 hours for adults. Every dog is different, so it helps to know your dog's usual interval from your logs."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "My outdoor-only dog hasn't gone all day. Is that okay?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Dogs often hold it because of the weather, but holding it a long time is hard on the body. Take them out even briefly, and if they strain and nothing comes out, go to the vet right away."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What illnesses can holding pee cause?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "It can make urinary tract infections, bladder infections and urinary stones more likely, and in serious cases it can strain the kidneys. Poop can harden and lead to constipation."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I skip the walk on a rainy day?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "You can skip the long walk, but still give them a potty chance. You can step out front briefly just to do their business, or use an indoor pad as a backup."
   }
  }
